{
  "tema": 6961,
  "slug": "imperativo-usted-ustedes-nosotros",
  "titulo": "Forming commands for usted, ustedes and nosotros",
  "subtitulo": "Firme aquí, no se preocupen, comamos: the present subjunctive does the work.",
  "foto": "t07.jpg",
  "regla": "Commands for usted, ustedes and nosotros, affirmative and negative, use the present subjunctive: hable, coman, comamos, no comamos.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "For **usted**, **ustedes** and **nosotros**, both affirmative and negative commands use the **present subjunctive**. Stem changes and spelling changes come along."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Person",
            "Affirmative",
            "Negative"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "usted",
              "firme aquí",
              "no firme aquí"
            ],
            [
              "ustedes",
              "coman",
              "no coman"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros (_let's_)",
              "comamos",
              "no comamos"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Nosotros**: the subjunctive says _let's_ or _let's not_: **¡Hagamos una fiesta!**, **¡No seamos egoístas!**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "In everyday speech, people often prefer **¿Por qué no…?** + present for _let's_ (**¿Por qué no vamos a la playa?**), and **Mejor no…** + present for _let's not_ (**Mejor no vamos**)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Usted / ustedes**: used in formal situations, in a bank, a store or with older people: **Firme aquí, por favor**. In Mexico **ustedes** is the only plural _you_, formal or not."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Pronouns are attached to the end in affirmative commands (**siéntese**, **sentémonos**) and go before in negative ones (**no se siente**)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: if it isn't **tú** saying yes, it's the subjunctive."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Ella no quiere que ==comamos== tan rápido.",
              "en": "She doesn't want us to eat so fast. (subjunctive)"
            },
            {
              "es": "¡==Comamos== más rápido!",
              "en": "Let's eat faster!"
            },
            {
              "es": "¡No ==comamos== tan rápido!",
              "en": "Let's not eat so fast!"
            },
            {
              "es": "¡==Limpiemos== el carro!",
              "en": "Let's clean the car!"
            },
            {
              "es": "¡==Tengamos== paciencia!",
              "en": "Let's be patient!"
            },
            {
              "es": "==Firme== aquí, por favor.",
              "en": "Sign here, please."
            },
            {
              "es": "No ==se preocupe==, ya le abro el carro.",
              "en": "Don't worry, I'll open the car for you."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Pasen== por aquí y ==esperen== un momento.",
              "en": "Come this way and wait a moment."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
